body: "## What happened\n\npm-changelog 2026.11.7 changed how entries inside a section are ordered. #324 (merged 2026-11-06) switched `compareItems` from the old item timestamp to the SDK's `resolveCompletionTimestamp`, so `completed_at` now wins over `closed_at`. The new order is the correct one. But:\n\n- The 2026.11.7 release notes list only three dependency bumps. The tracking item `pmc-total-item-order` is still `in_progress`, so the generator left it out of the release that shipped it.\n- Every consumer whose committed CHANGELOG.md has an item with `completed_at` earlier than `closed_at` failed `changelog:check` on its Dependabot pm-toolchain PR (2026.11.6 to 2026.11.7). On 2026-11-11 that was 16 repositories (pm-lint#72, pm-web#315, pm-starter#203, pm-slack#189, pm-brief#214, pm-todos#191, pm-csv#240, pm-jira#200, pm-gantt-chart#223, pm-context#221, pm-hypothesis#27, pm-linear#216, pm-presets#208, pm-graph#206, pm-jev#106, pm-ops#261). The diff is pure reordering, for example in pm-lint:\n\n```\n ### Other\n-- Publish pm-lint as @unbrained/pm-lint (... pm-lint-scoped-npm-name ...)   closed 10-30, completed 10-26\n - Release readiness behind PM_RELEASE_APPROVED (... pm-lint-release-gate ...) closed 10-27, completed 10-27\n+- Publish pm-lint as @unbrained/pm-lint (... pm-lint-scoped-npm-name ...)\n```\n\n- The failure message, \"Changelog is out of date\", reads like the consumer's tracker drifted. Nothing says the generator changed, or that one regeneration fixes it.\n\nVerified locally on pm-lint's toolchain branch: pm-changelog 2026.11.6 passes the check against the same SDK (2026.11.7) and the same pm binary, and 2026.11.7 fails it. So the change is in pm-changelog, not in pm-cli.\n\n## Asks\n\n1. Close `pmc-total-item-order` with its delivery evidence (#324, released in 2026.11.7), and record the ordering change for 2026.11.7 as a consumer-visible change with a one-line action: regenerate CHANGELOG.md once.\n2. Treat any change to rendered output as a consumer upgrade. Declare it in the consumer-upgrades contract, so `pm-changelog` can say what to do.\n3. Make `--check` tell generator drift apart from tracker drift. When the committed file matches what the previous rendering rules would produce from the same tracker, say \"the generator's rendering changed in <version>; run <the configured generate command> once\" instead of only \"out of date\".\n\nThe fleet now regenerates these PRs automatically (an hourly sweep on the orchestrator host). Consumers outside the fleet still get a confusing red check on every rendering change.\n\n\n---\n\n### GitHub comments (1)\n\n> **@coderabbitai[bot]** (2026-11-11T05:39:12Z)\n>\n> <!-- coderabbit-ai-generated:v1 -->\n> \n> <!-- This is an auto-generated issue plan by CodeRabbit -->\n> <details>\n> <summary>🔗 Related PRs</summary>\n> <dl>\n> <dd>\n> <br>\n> \n> unbraind/pm-changelog#324 - fix: keep section order stable across pm metadata writes [merged]\n> </dd>\n> </dl>\n> </details>\n> \n> ---\n> <details>\n> <summary>📝 Issue Planner</summary>\n> <dl>\n> <dd>\n> <br>\n> \n> <sub>Check the box below or use the `@coderabbitai plan` command to generate an implementation plan and prompts that you can use with your favorite coding assistant.</sub>\n> \n> - [ ] <!-- {\"checkboxId\":\"8d4f2b9c-3e1a-4f7c-a9b2-d5e8f1c4a7b9\"} --> Create Plan\n> </dd>\n> </dl>\n> </details>\n> \n> \n> ---\n> <details>\n> <summary> 🧪 Issue enrichment is currently in open beta.</summary>\n> <dl>\n> <dd>\n> <br>\n> \n> \n> You can configure auto-planning by selecting labels in the issue_enrichment configuration.\n> \n> To disable automatic issue enrichment, add the following to your `.coderabbit.yaml`:\n> ```yaml\n> issue_enrichment:\n>   auto_enrich:\n>     enabled: false\n> ```\n> </dd>\n> </dl>\n> </details>\n> \n> 💬 Have feedback or questions? Drop into our [discord](https://discord.gg/coderabbit)!"
